WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.317
This final slide gives you resources for continuing your Pandas learning.

00:00:04.317 --> 00:00:09.477
The official Pandas documentation should become a normal part of your workflow.

00:00:09.477 --> 00:00:14.762
You do not need to memorize every parameter.

00:00:14.762 --> 00:00:18.217
Learn the core patterns, and then use the documentation when you need details.

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:26.142
The Pandas user guide and the introductory tutorials are especially useful because they provide examples for

00:00:26.142 --> 00:00:32.452
selection, missing data, grouping, merging, reshaping, and many other common tasks.

00:00:32.452 --> 00:00:34.902
Your best next step is practice.

00:00:34.902 --> 00:00:40.637
Choose a small real CSV dataset and begin with a question, not with code.

00:00:40.637 --> 00:00:43.397
Write down what you want to learn from the data.

00:00:43.397 --> 00:00:50.442
Then load the file, inspect it, identify quality problems, clean only what needs to be cleaned,

00:00:50.442 --> 00:00:54.257
create useful transformations, summarize the result, and validate what you produced.

00:00:54.257 --> 00:01:00.852
That process is more valuable than memorizing a long list of functions.

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:06.972
In the next module, we can build on this foundation with more advanced Pandas workflows, reshaping,

00:01:06.972 --> 00:01:10.676
time-series analysis, and performance-oriented techniques.
